    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-git\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! Is it possible to rename :Git command to something like :MiniGit so that vim-fugitive can be used along with mini-git. I want mini-git show_at_cursor to work as it is while wanting the vim-fugitive's capabilities if possible. Can this be done in any way.",
