            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, no, it will stay the same.\r\n\r\nYou can still use `MiniGit.show_at_cursor()` (or probably even `require('mini.git').show_at_cursor()` without prior `require('mini.git').setup()`) even though `:Git` from 'mini.git' is not used. Besides, 'vim-fugitive' provides `:G` command which is [the same as its `:Git`](https://github.com/tpope/vim-fugitive/blob/0444df68cd1cdabc7453d6bd84099458327e5513/plugin/fugitive.vim#L547-L550).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
