            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I came across a similar problem recently when trying to migrate to use more vim-fugitive and keep using mini.git's `minigit_summary_string`.  Depending on the loading sequence, the `Git` command registered from mini.git could interact with vim-fugitive command / interface from time to time.\n\nOne solution I found was to delete \"Git\" command right after mini.git setup call.\n\n```\nrequire(\"mini.git\").setup()\npcall(vim.api.nvim_del_user_command, \"Git\")\n```",
